  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HANDS OPEN WIDE DEVELOPMENT INITIATIVE Relief for Displaced Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project proposed to work with the host community of Durumi and IDPs living in Durumi camp by addressing their humanitarian and protection need through the provision of food, non-food items, and capacity building to ameliorate negative coping strategy such as commercial sex work and related gender based violence.  The project is aligned with SDGs 1 and 2 and is to be implemented by directly by Hands Open Wide Development Initiatives (HOWDI).</narrative>
  </description>
